'''Kadhi''' or '''karhi''' is a yogurt-based dish originating from [[Rajasthan]], India.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Minwalla |first=Shabnam |date=2020-07-23 |title=Kadhi is India's comfort food |url=https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/blink/takeaway/kadhi-is-indias-comfort-food/article32176103.ece |access-date=2024-04-28 |website=Business Line |language=en |quote=It is widely believed that the kadhi originated in the deserts of Rajasthan, where cooks started using dairy products to supplement scarce vegetables |location=Chennai}}</ref> It is made by simmering [[yogurt]] with [[Gram flour|besan (gram flour)]] and [[List of Indian spices|spices]] until it forms a thick, tangy gravy.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Gill |first=Romy |date=28 October 2019 |title=Savoring the Taste of Memories in Northern India |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/28/travel/northern-india-food.html |access-date=2026-05-25 |work=The New York Times |language=en-US |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>  It is sometimes mixed with [[pakora]]s (deep-fried fritters).<ref>{{Cite web |last=Kale |first=Neha |date=4 May 2022 |title=Feels like home: 'This dish has made me cry on many, many occasions' |url=https://www.sbs.com.au/food/article/feels-like-home-this-dish-has-made-me-cry-on-many-many-occasions/2kx6osk2s |access-date=2026-05-25 |website=SBS Food |language=en}}</ref> It is often eaten with [[cooked rice]] or [[roti]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Besan Kadhi |url=https://food.ndtv.com/recipe-besan-kadhi-99117 |access-date=2024-05-11 |website=NDTV Food |language=en}}</ref>
